title: 'spec-msg: add primitives'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Adds the primitives for Speculative Messaging v0.5. The byte formats are in
    `docs/speculative-messaging-encoding-spec.md`.

    Relay-visible, in `polkadot-primitives::v9`:
    - `StreamsRoot` and `RequiresSet`. A `RequiresSet` is non-empty by construction.
    - New `UMPSignal::Provides` and `UMPSignal::Requires` variants, read through
      `CandidateUMPSignals`. `MAX_UMP_SIGNALS = 4` bounds `ump_signals()`: at most one
      signal of each variant.

    Parachain-side, in the new `cumulus-primitives-spec-messaging` crate: `StreamId`, the
    stream MMR, the `StreamsRoot` trie, lifts and `requires` synthesis, the message fetch
    protocol and its verifiers, channel and flow-control state, and the messaging inherent data.

    Nothing emits the new signals yet. `SchedulingSignals::from_block_signals` in
    `cumulus-primitives-core` panics if a parachain emits one, until a follow-up forwards them.
crates:
- name: polkadot-primitives
  bump: major
- name: cumulus-primitives-spec-messaging
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-primitives-test-helpers
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-sdk
  bump: minor
